Run these two next — they give the actual app list

A3e — Claims APM IDs across all namespaces

fetch dt.entity.host
| fields id, entity.name, tags, tagStr = toString(tags)
| filter contains(lower(tagStr), "claim")
| expand tags
| filter startsWith(tags, "APMID:")
   or startsWith(tags, "[Azure]APMID:")
   or startsWith(tags, "[Environment]APPID:")
   or startsWith(tags, "APP000")
   or startsWith(tags, "APP002")
| summarize hosts = countDistinctExact(id), by:{tags}
| sort hosts desc


A3f — normalized, one row per APM ID

fetch dt.entity.host
| fields id, entity.name, tags, tagStr = toString(tags)
| filter contains(lower(tagStr), "claim")
| expand tags
| filter contains(tags, "APP000") or contains(tags, "APP002")
| parse tags, "LD 'APP' INT:num"
| fieldsAdd apmid = concat("APP", toString(num))
| summarize hosts = countDistinctExact(id), by:{apmid}
| sort hosts desc


A3f is the deliverable — a deduped APM ID list with host counts, ready to join against your 152.

A3g — criticality + env profile of the Claims estate (small output, high value)

fetch dt.entity.host
| fields id, entity.name, tags, tagStr = toString(tags)
| filter contains(lower(tagStr), "claim")
| expand tags
| filter startsWith(tags, "BusinessCriticality:")
   or startsWith(tags, "CMDB_ENV:")
   or startsWith(tags, "OS_C:")
   or startsWith(tags, "DB_C:")
| summarize hosts = countDistinctExact(id), by:{tags}
| sort hosts desc
